# Perf harness: the SOURCES (wiremock mappings + generator, k6 scenarios,
# repo configs, nginx conf, scripts) are tracked — CI boots the stack from
# them. Only run OUTPUTS and rendered/secret files are ignored. Do NOT
# re-add a broad performance/*/* ignore: it silently kept the whole harness
# out of the repo and every perf workflow failed at checkout for months.
performance/results/*
!performance/results/.gitkeep
performance/wiremock/__files/*.bin*
performance/pantera-config.yml
performance/secrets/*.pem
performance/data/
performance/fixtures/uploads/*.tgz
performance/scripts/__pycache__/

# Working / transient analysis + audit directories — never committed.
# These hold model deliverables, scratch findings, internal RCA notes,
# perf-bench harness outputs, and design specs that are not part of the
# shipped product. Keep them on disk locally, but out of the repo so the
# tree stays tight for users / admins / devs.
analysis/
audit/
benchmark/
docs/analysis/
docs/superpowers/
